  "question": {
    "text": "If $x \\frac{d y}{d x}=y(\\log y-\\log x+1)$, then the solution of the equation is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "v7ziT",
      "text": "\n$y \\log \\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right)=c x$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "KUVRs",
      "text": "\n$x \\log \\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)=c y$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4BjBD",
      "text": "\n$\\log \\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)=c x$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "BVB4W",
      "text": "\n$\\log \\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right)=c y$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{x d y}{d x}=y(\\log y-\\log x+1) \\\\\n& \\frac{d y}{d x}=\\frac{y}{x}\\left(\\log \\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)+1\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nPut $y=v x$\n$\\frac{d y}{d x}=v+\\frac{x d v}{d x}$\n$\\Rightarrow v+\\frac{x d v}{d x}=v(\\log v+1)$\n$\\frac{x d v}{d x}=v \\log v$\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{d v}{v \\log v}=\\frac{d x}{x}$\nput $\\log v=z$\n$\\frac{1}{v} d v=d z$\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{d z}{z}=\\frac{d x}{x}$\n$\\ln z=\\ln x+\\ln c$\n$z=c x$\n$\\log v=c x$\n$\\log \\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)=c x$",
    "image": null
  },
